{"user": "how does it work this game?", "user_ts": "2026-08-05T12:37:17.908028+00:00", "assistant": "Othello/Reversi basics:\n\n- You are **Black**. On your turn, place a black disc on a **legal empty square** marked by a pale dot.\n- A move is legal if it **traps one or more White discs** in a straight line between your new black disc and another black disc.\n- Any trapped White discs are **flipped to Black**.\n- Then White moves the same way.\n- If a player has **no legal move**, they must **pass**.\n- When the board is full or neither player can move, the player with **more discs wins**.\n\nIn this endgame, don\u2019t just pick the move that flips the most now. Think about:\n- **Corners**: once taken, they can\u2019t be flipped.\n- **Squares next to empty corners** can be risky.\n- **Mobility**: leave White with few bad moves if possible.\n- Try to imagine the final disc count, not just this turn.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-05T12:37:19.978180+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-05T12:37:22.831686+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant": {"final": ["Direct Instruction"], "consensus": ["Direct Instruction"], "votes": {"Direct Instruction": 3, "Hint": 1}, "confidence": {"Direct Instruction": 1.0, "Hint": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Direct Instruction"], "llama": ["Direct Instruction", "Hint"], "sonnet": ["Direct Instruction"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["General Principle"], "consensus": ["General Principle"], "vot